/T (Problem - The Bottleneck)
/E (Problem - The Bottleneck)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
112 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 101 0 R
/E (Outpatient clinics face a persistent communication bottleneck caused by traditional phone-intake and paging workflows. Nurses spend an estimated 15% to 25% \(Clinical Communication and Collarboration Solutions, 2024\) of their shifts waiting on hold with operators instead of providing patient care. In a clinic with just two nurses, this results in approximately $21,000 per year wasted in lost productivity. As staffing shortages continue across healthcare, inefficient communication systems make it harder for clinics to respond quickly to patients while maintaining high-quality care.)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
113 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/P 101 0 R
/T (How PageMD Solves It)
/E (How PageMD Solves It)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
114 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 101 0 R
/E (PageMD addresses the clinic communication bottleneck by automatically answering and intelligently routing incoming calls through a conversational AI-powered paging system designed specifically for clinical workflows. Unlike traditional operator-based paging systems, PageMD can handle multiple calls simultaneously by creating parallel call-handling instances, eliminating hold times and reducing callback delays. It delivers structured, prioritized messages directly to providers and staff, allowing nurses to spend less time managing communication and more time with patients. This enables clinics to improve response speed, increase staff productivity, and expand patient access without increasing staffing costs.)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
